# GitHub Governance Document

## Version

Version: 2.0

Maintained By:
Raconsys Governance Team

---

# 1. Organization Structure

## Governance Hierarchy

Owner
↓
Release Manager
↓
Tech Lead
↓
Developer

---

## Owner Responsibilities

Owners are responsible for:

* Repository Governance
* Security Policies
* Branch Protection Rules
* GitHub Actions Governance
* Secrets Management
* Team Management
* Repository Administration

Owners have full administrative access.

Number of Owners should be limited.

Recommended:

* Owner 1
* Owner 2

---

## Release Manager Responsibilities

Release Managers are responsible for:

* Production Release Approval
* Stage → Main Approval
* Release Monitoring
* Client Delivery Validation
* Audit Report Review

---

## Tech Lead Responsibilities

Tech Leads are responsible for:

* Code Review
* Feature Validation
* Develop → Stage Approval
* Technical Quality Assurance
* Team Guidance

---

## Developer Responsibilities

Developers are responsible for:

* Feature Development
* Bug Fixes
* Pull Requests
* Unit Testing
* Code Reviews

---

# 2. Account Naming Standard

## GitHub Username Standard

Format:

companyname-dev-name

Examples:

scrumiq-dev-subhu

scrumiq-dev-pramod

scrumiq-dev-rakesh

---

## Branch Naming Standard

Feature:

feature/<feature-name>

Examples:

feature/login-page

feature/user-management

---

Bug Fix:

bugfix/<issue-name>

Examples:

bugfix/payment-calculation

bugfix/login-validation

---

Hotfix:

hotfix/<issue-name>

Examples:

hotfix/production-login-failure

hotfix/payment-crash

---

# 3. Repository Branch Strategy

## Branch Structure

feature/*
↓
develop
↓
stage
↓
main

---

## Branch Purpose

### feature/*

Development Branch

Used for:

* New Features
* Enhancements
* Bug Fixes

---

### develop

Integration Branch

Used for:

* Team Integration
* Feature Consolidation
* Internal Testing

---

### stage

Pre-Production Branch

Used for:

* QA Testing
* UAT Validation
* Security Verification

---

### main

Production Branch

Used for:

* Production Releases
* Client Deliveries

---

# 4. Permission Matrix

| Activity              | Developer | Tech Lead | Release Manager | Owner |
| --------------------- | --------- | --------- | --------------- | ----- |
| Create Feature Branch | Yes       | Yes       | Yes             | Yes   |
| Push Feature Branch   | Yes       | Yes       | Yes             | Yes   |
| Create PR             | Yes       | Yes       | Yes             | Yes   |
| Approve Develop PR    | No        | Yes       | Yes             | Yes   |
| Approve Stage PR      | No        | Yes       | Yes             | Yes   |
| Approve Main PR       | No        | No        | Yes             | Yes   |
| Merge To Develop      | No        | Yes       | Yes             | Yes   |
| Merge To Stage        | No        | Yes       | Yes             | Yes   |
| Merge To Main         | No        | No        | Yes             | Yes   |
| Modify Branch Rules   | No        | No        | No              | Yes   |
| Manage Secrets        | No        | No        | No              | Yes   |
| Modify Actions        | No        | No        | No              | Yes   |
| Manage Teams          | No        | No        | No              | Yes   |

---

# 5. Branch Protection Rules

## Develop Branch

Rules:

* Pull Request Required
* Minimum 1 Approval
* No Force Push
* No Direct Push
* Conversation Resolution Required

Approver:

Tech Lead

---

## Stage Branch

Rules:

* Pull Request Required
* Minimum 1 Approval
* No Force Push
* No Direct Push
* Conversation Resolution Required
* Branch Must Be Up To Date

Approver:

Release Manager

---

## Main Branch

Rules:

* Pull Request Required
* Minimum 2 Approvals
* No Force Push
* No Direct Push
* Conversation Resolution Required
* Branch Must Be Up To Date
* Required Status Checks Enabled

Approvers:

Release Manager
Owner

---

# 6. GitHub Actions Policy

GitHub Actions shall be used for:

* Build Generation
* Governance Logging
* Delivery Logging
* Client Repository Synchronization
* Future CI/CD Automation

---

## Workflow Storage

All workflows shall be stored in:

.github/workflows

---

## Workflow Modification

Only Owners may:

* Create Workflows
* Modify Workflows
* Delete Workflows

---

# 7. Logging & Audit Policy

## Governance Report

Generated automatically on:

Pull Request Merge

Captures:

* PR Number
* PR Title
* Author
* Reviewer
* Merge Information
* Repository
* Branch
* Commit Information

---

## Client Delivery Report

Generated automatically on:

Client Delivery

Captures:

* Source Repository
* Target Repository
* Source Commit
* Client Commit
* Delivery Status
* Workflow Information
* Delivery Timestamp

---

## Report Retention

Minimum Retention:

90 Days

Future Enhancement:

Central Audit Repository

---

# 8. Client Delivery Governance

## Client Access Policy

Clients shall have access only to:

Client Repository

Clients shall not have access to:

* Source Repository
* Develop Branch
* Stage Branch
* GitHub Actions
* Secrets
* Governance Settings

---

## Delivery Method

GitHub Actions

Authentication Method:

CLIENT_REPO_TOKEN

Stored As:

GitHub Repository Secret

---

# 9. Build Delivery Policy

## Delivery Principle

Only Build Artifacts shall be delivered.

Source Code shall not be delivered.

---

## Approved Deliverables

React:

dist/

Angular:

dist/

Spring Boot:

app.jar

Release Documentation:

release-report.txt

delivery-report.txt

---

## Prohibited Deliverables

Source Files:

src/

GitHub Configuration:

.github/

Feature Branch Content

Development Configuration Files

Internal Governance Documents

---

# 10. Release Workflow

Developer
↓
Feature Branch

feature/*
↓
Pull Request

develop
↓
Approval

stage
↓
Approval

main
↓
GitHub Actions

Build Generation
↓
Client Delivery
↓
Delivery Report
↓
Audit Storage

---

